                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="572-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="572-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="572-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ></span>Avantone Pro CV-28</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The CV-28 is a small-diaphragm tube condenser with three interchangeable capsules providing three pickup patterns: cardioid, omni, and hypercardioid. Unlike related multipattern SDCs, only the internal capsule is changed &#8212; the external grille assembly must be removed first, to expose the threaded capsule head.</p><p>The diaphragm in these capsules measures 6 microns in thickness, with an approximate diaphragm diameter (measured by us within the inside diameter of the trim ring at the top of the capsule assembly) of 17mm.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/avant/CV28-circuit.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/avant/CV28-circuit-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="CV-28 Circuit" width="200" /></a>The microphone shares exterior metalwork with a few other models, such as the Advanced Audio CM-28, the Groove Tubes GT44, and the Sterling ST44. However, the GT44 and ST44 circuits differ considerably from the CV-28. Further, the capsule mounting platform on the ST44/GT44 is slightly different than the CV-28.</p><p>The tube is a 6J1B, a Chinese-made tube sourced by the manufacturer. The transformer is also of Chinese origin.</p><p>The mic includes a padded wooden box, suspension shockmount, dedicated power supply, power cable, 3 interchangeable capsules (omni, cardioid, hypercardioid) within a plastic pillbox, an aluminum flightcase, and a 5-year warranty.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Avant/CV-28">Avantone Pro CV-28</a> is also known as: CV28.</p><p>The mic was released in 2006.</p>
